Choose integer production x,y >=0. Resource A uses a[0]*x+a[1]*y, B uses b[0]*x+b[1]*y; capacities correspond to A,B. Each product has its own upper limit. Maximize profit[0]*x+profit[1]*y. Ties: smallest x, then smallest y. Report x, y and profit.
Inputs (all synthetic): {"a": [5, 2], "b": [4, 1], "capacity": [38, 23], "profit": [14, 23], "limits": [9, 9]}
Required answer keys: x, y, profit. Return a JSON object of numeric values using submit. Use at least 6 significant digits; tolerance max(0.0001, 0.00001*abs(target)). Full reward requires every key correct, no extra keys. Partial credit is at most 0.15 and only for correct numeric subresults. You may run Python calculations first. Check units and assumptions. No intermediate correctness feedback.

