Price a fixed-coupon bond between coupon dates. Annual coupon and annual nominal yield are fractions; yield compounds frequency times/year. remaining_periods includes the next coupon and final redemption. elapsed_fraction is fraction of current coupon period already elapsed, so next payment occurs in (1-elapsed_fraction)/frequency years. Use fractional-exponent discounting; accrued interest=coupon_per_period*elapsed_fraction. Report dirty price, clean price and Macaulay duration in years.
